## ✅ Final Instruction to Append

```
Confirm at the end that:
- Every one of the 15 features from the architecture spec has a real, connected
  screen — list them and check each one off.
- No component contains hardcoded sample/mock data.
- The white + #F50A70 palette is defined once as design tokens and reused
  everywhere, not redefined per component.
- Every screen has real loading, empty, and error states tied to actual API calls.
```

---

### How to use this prompt
Paste the **Context** block + **Master Instruction** + **Final Instruction** into your AI coding assistant (or Claude Code) in one message. It already has the architecture spec and backend structure in context, so it can generate the full frontend — design system, layout shell, and all 15 feature screens — wired live to your real backend in one pass.